      "side": 1,
      "message": "The FIPS140 module consists of code that gets built into the core kernel as well, and it gets built a second time with BUILD_FIPS140_KO set. So there has to be a shared #include *somewhere*, that picks a different definition when rebuilding the code. So it is going to be something like this, or something based on -include fips140.h on the compiler command line, but this would involve making these #define\u0027s conditional rather than the fips140.h ones (and having the code in asm/alternative-macros.h at least makes it obvious to anyone applying changes here that there is a third definition which needs to remain in sync)",
